# Example crontab line for infra/postgres/backup.sh - not read by anything, a reference to
# copy from. Cron itself is not version-controlled, so this file documents the line the same
# way .env.example documents .env.
#
# Install with: crontab -e (as whichever user has access to the repo checkout and Docker),
# then paste a line like this, with the real path to the checkout:
#
# 0 3 * * * cd /opt/century-road-backend && bash infra/postgres/backup.sh >> /var/log/century-road-backup.log 2>&1
#
# Called through "bash", not "./infra/postgres/backup.sh" directly - this repo is edited on
# Windows, where the executable bit does not reliably survive a checkout/commit round trip
# (see the release workflow's own CRLF notes), so this does not depend on it.
#
# Daily at 03:00 server time. stdout/stderr both go to the logfile, since cron silently
# discards them otherwise: a broken backup you never hear about is worse than a noisy log.
